{"version": 2, "width": 100, "height": 34, "title": "BoundedCode evidence demo"}
[0.010131, "o", "\u001b[2mBoundedCode evidence demo. Controlled fixture: demo/evidence/testdata/shop.\r\nModel: SCRIPTED stand-in (fixed commands in demo/evidence/scripted-agent.txt), not a real model. The rest is the real product.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;36m# 1. The bug: 10 items should get the 10% bulk discount (900 cents)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.005328, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m go run ./cmd/quote 10\r\n"]
[1.586135, "o", "10 items at 100 cents: total 1000 cents\r\n"]
[1.58711, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.587112, "o", "\u001b[1;36m# 2. The existing tests pass anyway\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.588441, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m go test ./...\r\n"]
[3.197838, "o", "ok  \texample.com/shop\t0.001s\r\n?   \texample.com/shop/cmd/quote\t[no test files]\r\n"]
[3.199218, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m# 3. Ask BoundedCode to fix it\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[4.206535, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m bcode task create \"Orders of exactly 10 items do not get the 10% bulk discount: go run ./cmd/quote 10 prints a total of 1000 cents, but it should be 900.\" -c 'go test ./... passes' --run\r\n"]
[4.744365, "o", "using openai-compatible model scripted-agent (working context 32768 tokens)\r\n"]
